{# DRAFT 1 — minimal reaction rules
   PLACEHOLDERS: followerInterruption and nonFollowerInterruption are proposed
   integer settings. Replace these field names with the actual decorators.
#}
[ system ]
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set followerInterruption = default(ss.followerInterruption, 3) %}
{% set nonFollowerInterruption = default(ss.nonFollowerInterruption, 2) %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

{% set hasExchange = existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{% set playerSpoke = hasExchange and lastSpeaker.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerWasAddressed = hasExchange and lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = false %}
{% if playerSpoke and not is_follower(lastDialogueTarget.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% elif playerWasAddressed and not is_follower(lastSpeaker.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% endif %}

# Task

An NPC has just spoken to a recipient. Select one NPC to react, or select `0` so no NPC speaks.

Output exactly one of:

- `0`
- `[exact candidate name]>[exact target name]`
- `[exact candidate name]>player`

No explanation or other text.

# Rules that always apply

- `0` is always allowed.
- Never select {{ lastSpeaker.name }}. That person just spoke.
- Never select someone merely because they are nearby.
- Never select anyone to comment that the player is silent or slow to answer.
- The person who was addressed is the ordinary next speaker when a response is warranted.
- Anyone else is entering an exchange that did not address them and needs a reason permitted below.
- Select at most one speaker.

{% if playerNonFollowerExchange %}
# Follower interruption setting

These instructions apply only to followers entering the current exchange between the player and a non-follower.

{% if followerInterruption == 1 %}
Do not select a follower. Interjection, personality, `[FOLLOWER]`, and `[ENGAGED]` do not override this.
{% elif followerInterruption == 2 %}
Select a follower only if the last line addressed or referred to that follower, their role requires a response to this exchange, or their Interjection text names a specific friend, family member, lover, or rival who was just discussed. General topic matches do not qualify.
{% elif followerInterruption == 3 %}
Select a follower for the reasons allowed at the previous position, for any clear match in their Interjection text, or to warn, object, de-escalate, or escalate an actual argument, threat, or fight shown in the recent dialogue.
{% elif followerInterruption == 4 %}
Select a follower for the reasons allowed at the previous position, when the recent events show a decision that affects them, or when their profile gives a reason tied specifically to the last line.
{% else %}
Use the recent dialogue, short profile, Interjection text, and personality to decide freely whether a follower would enter this exchange. Mere presence, follower status, and the player's delay are still not reasons.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Non-follower interruption setting

These instructions apply only to non-followers other than the last speaker and the person who was addressed.

{% if nonFollowerInterruption == 1 %}
Do not select an unrelated non-follower. Interjection and `[ENGAGED]` do not override this.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 2 %}
Select an unrelated non-follower only if the last line addressed or referred to them, their role requires a response to this exchange, or their Interjection text names a specific person who was just discussed. General topic matches do not qualify.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 3 %}
Select an unrelated non-follower for the reasons allowed at the previous position, for any clear match in their Interjection text, or to warn, object, de-escalate, or escalate an actual conflict shown in the recent dialogue.
{% else %}
Select an unrelated non-follower for the reasons allowed at the previous position or when their profile gives a reason tied specifically to the last line. Mere presence and the player's delay are still not reasons.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

# Choosing `0`

Choose `0` when the addressed person is the player and no permitted interruption is strong enough to take the floor.

Otherwise choose `0` when the addressed candidate does not need to respond and no other candidate has a reason allowed by the applicable interruption instructions.

{{ get_scene_context(0, 0, "full") }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
# Recent Dialogue

{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Current Exchange

**{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke to {{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}.**
{% endif %}

# Candidates

{% for candidate in candidateDialogues %}
{% if candidate.UUID and candidate.UUID != 0 %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(candidate.UUID) %}
{{ candidate.id }}. **{{ cinfo.name }}**{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastDialogueTarget.UUID %} **[ADDRESSED]**{% endif %}{% if hasExchange and candidate.UUID == lastSpeaker.UUID %} **[JUST SPOKE — DO NOT SELECT]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) %} **[FOLLOWER]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagEngaged and is_in_package(candidate.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} **[ENGAGED]**{% endif %}{% if not cinfo.isVirtual and tagInScene and (is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction") or is_in_faction(candidate.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction")) %} **[IN SCENE]**{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %} **[VIRTUAL NPC]**{% endif %}
   - {% if not cinfo.isVirtual %}{{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(candidate.distance) }}m — {% endif %}{{ render_character_profile("short_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
   - **Interjection:** {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", candidate.UUID) }}
{% if playerNonFollowerExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and is_follower(candidate.UUID) and followerInterruption >= 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% elif hasExchange and not cinfo.isVirtual and not is_follower(candidate.UUID) and candidate.UUID != lastSpeaker.UUID and candidate.UUID != lastDialogueTarget.UUID and nonFollowerInterruption == 4 %}
   - **Personality:** {{ render_character_profile("bio_personality", candidate.UUID) }}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

# Targeting

{% if playerSpoke %}
- If `[ADDRESSED]` responds, target `player`.
{% else %}
- If `[ADDRESSED]` responds, target {{ lastSpeaker.name }}.
{% endif %}
- An interruption normally targets the person whose line caused the reaction.
- Use `player` only when the selected NPC is genuinely addressing the player.
- Regular NPCs cannot hear Virtual NPCs and cannot respond directly to them.
- A Virtual NPC may speak, but only another Virtual NPC may be its target.
- Always provide one exact target.

`[ENGAGED]` never overrides an interruption setting. Strongly avoid `[IN SCENE]` unless that candidate was directly addressed.

# Output examples

- `0`
- `Lydia>player`
- `Ulfric Stormcloak>Galmar Stone-Fist`

Do not add formatting, race, gender, explanation, or shortened names.

Output:
[ end user ]
